                            <comment id="495160" author="sebastien" created="Thu, 28 May 2026 13:39:08 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=defazio" class="user-hover" rel="defazio"&gt;defazio&lt;/a&gt;, thanks for pushing the patch &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/66224" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/66224&lt;/a&gt; on b2_17. I have assigned this ticket to you then.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495380" author="JIRAUSER19627" created="Tue, 2 Jun 2026 10:56:26 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Hi, I am not sure about the status of this patch. However, I would like to report that I have managed to build and test successfully a lustre client RPM with the attached  spec file. If that helps. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  &lt;span class="nobr"&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/attachment/64901/64901_magklaraslustrecliebt2170-5.spec" title="magklaraslustrecliebt2170-5.spec attached to LU-20312"&gt;magklaraslustrecliebt2170-5.spec&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class="rendericon" src="https://jira.whamcloud.com/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif" height="7" width="7" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would of course have liked to use the upstream Lustre patch for &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20312" title="backport kernel 6.16 compatibility to 2.17" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20312"&gt;LU-20312&lt;/a&gt; once available/backported. However, time is of essence for us and we need to security patch our systems with the latest and the greatest. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The latest RHEL 10.2 kernel: 6.12.0-211.18.1.el10_2.x86_64 #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu May 21 10:24:38 EDT 2026 x86_64 GNU/Linux&lt;br/&gt;
seems to brake 'timer_container_of(...)'. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The upstream kernel change is visible as “treewide, timers: Rename from_timer() to timer_container_of()”, committed in 2025 for the 6.16 development cycle. Red Hat appears to have backported this interface change into RHEL 10.2’s 6.12 kernel stream; other out-of-tree modules are reporting the same RHEL 9.8/RHEL 10.2 breakage. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Just my two cents here. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PS: We have tested this in a non o2ib ldiskfs install: (--with-o2ib=no --disable-server). However, the patch should work for other configuration combinations. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;#8211;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Georgios Magklaras PhD&lt;br/&gt;
Chief Engineer&lt;br/&gt;
IT Infrastructure/HPC&lt;br/&gt;
The Norwegian Meteorological Institute&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.met.no/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://www.met.no/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://www.steelcyber.com/georgioshome/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://www.steelcyber.com/georgioshome/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="495393" author="defazio" created="Tue, 2 Jun 2026 16:28:58 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Thanks &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=georgiosm" class="user-hover" rel="georgiosm"&gt;georgiosm&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We decided to back-port this patch for the same reason, due to the timer_containter_of change in RHEL 10.2.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We've built this for TOSS 6, based on RHEL 10.2, but it hasn't been run on our systems yet. For us the build includes a server build using zfs and o2ib and kfilnd.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496324" author="JIRAUSER21301" created="Wed, 17 Jun 2026 20:11:50 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=defazio" class="user-hover" rel="defazio"&gt;defazio&lt;/a&gt; given that 2.18 is LTS the question is do we still need to backport this to 2.17 ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="497103" author="ofaaland" created="Tue, 30 Jun 2026 23:30:50 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=voratovsky" class="user-hover" rel="voratovsky"&gt;voratovsky&lt;/a&gt; we need some Lustre client and server for our RHEL10 based distro, TOSS 6.  We can't wait until 2.18.0 is tagged, unfortunately.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the client, we want it to be as reliable as possible.  It will be used for production data in the next couple of months.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the server, we may be able to put off production servers until 2.18.0 has arrived.  But we will still need a server in TOSS 6 so that we can get HA working, verify our configuration management and scripts for monitoring and managing Lustre clusters, and do realistic ZFS testing.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
